 top of the `llama.cpp` fork point **`790cf51aa`**. It introduces:
*   **Performance:** RDNA-specific kernels (WMMA Flash Attention0.56.375.498 I slot print_timing: id  0 | task 0 | n_gen =    159, tg =  19.39 t/s, tg_3s =  19.34 t/s
, Gated-Delta-Net), fused MoE operations, and k-quant decode paths.
*   **Memory Efficiency:** An "attention-memory campaign" (Block 15) freeing ~3.4 GiB VRAM on large models (e.g., Qwen4exp) and ~800 MiB0.59.402.749 I slot print_timing: id  0 | task 0 | n_gen =    226, tg =  20.13 t/s, tg_3s =  22.13 t/s
